  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> characteristics of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></math> junction diode in forward bias is shown in the figure. The ratio of dynamic resistance, corresponding to forward bias voltage of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> respective is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/41e3a4ad-f94b-4662-a6a4-de8085e81d64-image.png\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 166px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
